---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Exhibits from '../components/Exhibits.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
const news = [
  ['Oct 2026', 'Keynote, 6th International SDG Conference, Chitrakoot: "Who Consulted the Village?"'],
  ['2026', 'Full paper accepted at CHI PLAY 2026: Proteus Card Deck, with Oliver Schneider and Mark Hancock.'],
  ['2026', 'Published at ACM Interactive Health 2026: "Embed, don\'t isolate", on stigma-sensitive parent dashboards.'],
  ['2026', 'Chapter "A/B Testing IRL" forthcoming from Springer.'],
  ['Oct 2025', 'PhD defended, University of Waterloo.'],
];
---
<Base title="Ali Rizvi">
  <section class="intro">
    <div class="intro-grid">
      <div class="text">
        <p class="label status">HCI researcher · PhD, University of Waterloo, 2025 · Where good problems take me</p>
        <h1>Ali Rizvi</h1>
        <p class="tagline">My teams and I build cool things.</p>
        <p>I'm a human-computer interaction researcher. I study what happens to technology when it leaves the room it was designed in and lands somewhere small, moving, or improvised: a van, a classroom, a card table. I build the systems as part of the research, and twice now the research has become a company. My work is published at CHI, Graphics Interface, CHI PLAY, and ACM Interactive Health.</p>
        <p>Before the doctorate I spent seven years in product and analytics, most recently owning the orchestration layer of Amazon Alexa, and before that leading data and AI solutions for compliance at Morgan Stanley. At Waterloo I taught nine courses in UX and HCI to about 700 students. I'm currently an independent researcher, and I'm on the academic job market for 2027.</p>
        <p class="label"><a href="/cv.pdf">CV (PDF)</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href="/research/">Research statement</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href="mailto:hello@arizvi.com">hello@arizvi.com</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="photo"><img src="/media/headshot.jpg" alt="Ali Rizvi" width="400" height="500" /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Section label="Research to company" title="A path, twice">
    <div class="grid"><p class="span-8">Each of these began as a question in the PhD, became a study and a paper, then an artefact, and then a company that keeps the field site open. The same path, with the same people, is what I'd bring to a department.</p></div>
    <Exhibits />
  </Section>

  <Section label="News">
    <ul class="news">
      {news.map(([d, t]) => <li><p class="label">{d}</p><p>{t}</p></li>)}
    </ul>
  </Section>
</Base>
